3	// Standalone, no-network, no-dependency check that a room's ROUND is decided
4	// once and handed to every member unchanged — the property SuperDraft's online
5	// fairness rests on (each player used to draw their own slot constraints
6	// client-side and then be scored against the other's lineup).
7	//
8	// index.js needs express/socket.io/cors, which aren't installed for a test run,
9	// so this stubs them through Module._load the way a test double would, stubs
10	// global fetch with the Django round payloads, then drives the real relay:
11	//   1. two players identify and queue for superdraft -> a room is created,
12	//   2. assert BOTH received roundData and the slot constraints are identical
13	//      (captures are deep-cloned, so this is a real comparison of two payloads
14	//      and not of one shared object reference with itself),
15	//   3. assert a reconnect (index.js's resumeMatch snapshot) re-serves the same
16	//      round, and that the retained payload is config-sized, not the pool,
17	//   4. same for contexto's secret.
18	//
19	// Run:  node scripts/sim_round_fanout.js     (exit code 0 = pass)
